---
import Shell from '../../layouts/Shell.astro';
import LegalNav from '../../components/LegalNav.astro';

// Written against the code rather than from a template. Every claim here is checkable: the
// permissions and the two hosts are in apps/extension/wxt.config.ts, and the storage calls are in
// apps/extension/utils/prefsStorage.ts — preferences go to storage.sync with storage.local as the
// fallback, and everything else is storage.session.

const updated = 'August 19, 2026';
---
<Shell
	title='Privacy — ArenaSwap'
	description='The ArenaSwap privacy notice: the preferences the extension retains, the information it transmits, the browser permissions it requests, and the treatment of this website.'
	path='legal/privacy/'
>
	<div class='container'>
		<div class='page-head'>
			<h1 class='page-title'>Privacy.</h1>
		</div>

		<div class='reading-shell'>
			<LegalNav current='legal/privacy/' />

			<div class='prose'>
				<p class='legal-updated'>Last updated {updated}</p>

				<h2>Information the extension retains</h2>
				<p>
					The extension retains the preferences you set. These comprise the leagues you follow,
					the teams you have marked as favorites, your sensitivity, cooldown and switch delay
					settings, your Standby Stream threshold, and the manner in which the score is composed.
					Your browser holds these preferences as it holds your bookmarks, and may accordingly
					make them available to you on any other computer at which you are signed in to the same
					browser profile.
				</p>
				<p>
					All other information belongs to the browsing session in which it arises and is
					discarded when that session ends. This comprises the tabs you have assigned to
					particular games, the tab you have designated as your Standby Stream, any manual
					adjustment you have applied to a game, and the recent scoring history from which the
					charts are drawn.
				</p>
				<p>
					The extension does not retain your name, your address, an account, a contact detail or
					any other particular by which you may be identified. No such particular is requested of
					you at any point.
				</p>

				<h2>Information the extension transmits</h2>
				<p>
					The extension communicates with two hosts, both of them operated by ESPN, and it is
					capable of reaching no others:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><code>site.api.espn.com</code>, for scores, schedules, game clocks, odds and win probabilities.</li>
					<li><code>a.espncdn.com</code>, for team crests and league marks.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					These are ordinary requests for information that ESPN publishes openly. ESPN therefore
					receives your network address and a record of the league scoreboards requested, precisely
					as it would were you to visit its website yourself. The extension attaches to those
					requests no identifier, no account and no personal information whatever. Where you
					disable a league in Settings, the extension ceases to request that league at all.
				</p>

				<h2>Browser permissions</h2>
				<p>
					The extension requests three permissions of your browser, and each is exercised only for
					the purpose stated:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Tabs.</strong> To present the tabs you have open, so that you may assign games
						to them, and to switch, mute and unmute those tabs. This permission conveys the list
						of tabs and nothing further. No part of the extension runs within the pages you visit.
					</li>
					<li><strong>Storage.</strong> To retain the preferences described above.</li>
					<li><strong>Notifications.</strong> To inform you that a switch has occurred. Your browser composes and displays each notification, and nothing leaves your computer in the process.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>This website</h2>
				<p>
					This website sets no cookies, employs no analytics and carries no tracking of any
					description, and requests your consent to nothing because there is nothing to consent
					to. It is hosted by GitHub Pages, and GitHub records requests made to its servers in the
					ordinary course of providing that hosting. The typefaces are served from this website
					rather than from any third party.
				</p>
				<p>
					Two features of this website do communicate with ESPN from your browser. The
					demonstration screens request team crests from <code>a.espncdn.com</code>, and the
					<a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}powerscore/`}>PowerScore page</a> scores games in
					progress and therefore requests live scoreboards for so long as you leave it open.
				</p>

				<h2>Children</h2>
				<p>
					The extension collects no personal information from any person of any age, and this
					includes children under the age of thirteen.
				</p>

				<h2>Modifications to this notice</h2>
				<p>
					This notice may be revised from time to time. A revision takes effect upon publication,
					and the date stated above records when this notice was last revised. Your continued use
					of the extension after publication constitutes your acceptance of the notice as revised.
				</p>

				<h2>Questions</h2>
				<p>
					Questions concerning this notice may be directed to the project's
					<a href='https://github.com/hiteacheryouare/arenaswap/issues'>issue tracker on GitHub</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</Shell>
